title: 'P8-D83: re-cut the critical anchor budget at human cadence and evaluate a cheaper flush'
summary: The founder chose to measure critical log entries at human cadence (about 1 per second alongside bulk load) instead of 1-in-64, and to have Aegis judge whether a cheaper ordering flush (F_BARRIERFSYNC, or plain fsync) suffices for critical commits. The 25 ms critical p99 budget is kept.
